<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Paris</h1><p class="st-meta">511 CE – 567 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Merovingian kingdom centred on Paris, created when Clovis' realm was divided among his sons in 511.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> in 511 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a> was shared among his four sons. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert I</a> received the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a> coast and later parts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert</a> ruled for nearly fifty years, campaigning against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-burgundians">Kingdom of the Burgundians</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, from where he brought back relics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vincent-of-saragossa">Saint Vincent</a>. For them he founded the abbey later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-germain-des-pres">Saint-Germain-des-Prés</a>. He joined his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> in murdering their nephews, the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer of Orléans</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert</a> died without sons in 558, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> briefly reunited the Frankish lands. In 561 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> passed to Chlothar's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charibert-i">Charibert I</a>, and after Charibert's death in 567 his kingdom was divided among his brothers, with Paris shared between them.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-paris.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Paris" width="320" height="215"><figcaption>Image: Limbourg Brothers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>511 CE – 567 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Childebert I, Charibert I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Frankish, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=539&amp;focus=kingdom-of-paris" aria-label="Kingdom of Paris on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Paris lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=539&amp;focus=kingdom-of-paris">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
